      "evidence": [
        "practice-cycle/SKILL.md lines 44-50: 'When a Principal message changes the active target, hard boundary, concept relation, authority, or acceptance condition, treat the former reading as invalid before another mutation. State the rejected assumption, new invariant, affected surfaces, and smallest disconfirming next probe.'",
        "practice-cycle/workbench-hooks.ts lines 88-96: 'Only if it revises an assumption or constraint of a still-active task—including its target, hard boundary, concept relation, authority, or acceptance condition—run practice-cycle continue and record one correction.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The blog UI task is still active, and the Principal's message changes the scope boundary and invalidates the prior implementation assumption. The former reading must be treated as invalid, and a correction receipt should be recorded with --rejected-assumption, --new-invariant, --affected-surface, and --next-probe."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Scenario B is a task switch, not a correction, because the prior task was completed and handed off before the new reevaluation began.",
      "evidence": [
        "practice-cycle/workbench-hooks.ts lines 96-98: 'Starting a new task after the prior task was completed, paused, or handed off is not a correction. Otherwise proceed without ceremony.'",
        "practice-cycle/CHANGELOG.md lines 31-34: '[workbench.intervention] Distinguish task switches from corrections — the intervention reminder records a correction only when a Principal message revises an assumption or constraint of a still-active task.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The DeepSeek model reevaluation is a new task started after the blog UI task was completed and handed off. No correction receipt is recorded; the new task proceeds as a fresh task switch."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Scenario C is ordinary continuation because the Principal's 'continue' message leaves the active reevaluation decision unchanged.",
      "evidence": [
        "practice-cycle/SKILL.md lines 50-52: 'Do not create a receipt for an ordinary execute, continue, or formatting request that leaves the active decision unchanged.'",
        "practice-cycle/workbench-hooks.ts lines 88-90: 'Only if it revises an assumption or constraint of a still-active task... run practice-cycle continue and record one correction.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The reevaluation remains active and unchanged; 'continue' is an ordinary execute/continue request. No correction receipt is created, and no decision-changing inheritance is recorded."
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Whether the blog UI task in Scenario A had any runtime receipt binding installed at the time of the Principal message; if so, the correction fields should also be recorded there, but the binding is optional evidence and never changes the skill's judgment or human authority (SKILL.md lines 48-50).",
    "Whether the DeepSeek reevaluation in Scenario B later revises an assumption of its own still-active task; that would be a separate correction event, not part of the initial task switch."
  ],
